To make the script robust we add the "" to the List variable.
if [[ "${List[$i]}" == *.txt ]]
This treats everything inside as 1 string.

The next stage of this level is to copy the scripts that end in txt to the backup folder.
We can use the copy command for this.
The full complete code is:
        #!/bin/bash
        
        List=($(ls -a))
        count=${#List[@]}
        
        for (( i = 0 ; i < count ; i++))
        do
        
                if [[ "${List[$i]}" == *.txt ]]
                then
                        cp "${List[$i]}" ../Backup/
                        echo "Txt file : "${List[$i]}" Has been copied"
                else
                        echo "No txt file: ${List[$i]}"
                fi
        done
